# config.example/syncthing/compose.env - syncthing's interpolation values that are not shared.
#
# syncthing's compose file interpolates only BIND_ADDR and TAILSCALE_ADDR, both shared
# per-host facts that live once in outpost.env, so this service adds nothing of its own to
# the interpolation pool. The file is a header only, for the same reason as 00_proxy's:
# `just up syncthing` feeds docker compose both --env-file lines and both must resolve.
#
# Per-server differences (device IDs, timezone, sync folders, host network mode) are not in
# this file but in the gitignored docker-compose.override.yml in the service dir, which
# docker compose auto-merges. Copy template_docker-compose.override.yml to start; see readme.
